<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="ProgId" content="Word.Document"><meta name="Generator" content="QuranNotes"><title>Noor RAG Executive Technical Guide</title><style>@page{margin:0.8in}body{font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#172033;line-height:1.5}h1{color:#0f3d34;font-size:24pt}h2{color:#12615a;font-size:16pt;border-bottom:1px solid #d8e4e1;padding-bottom:4pt}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}th,td{border:1px solid #cdd6df;padding:6pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}th{background:#eef6f4}.callout{background:#eef8f5;border-left:4pt solid #1b8a78;padding:10pt}.flow{font-family:Courier New,monospace;background:#f5f7fa;border:1px solid #dce3ea;padding:9pt;white-space:pre-wrap}code{font-family:Courier New,monospace;background:#f0f4f7}.muted{color:#667085}</style></head><body><h1>QuranNotes Noor RAG — Executive Technical Design &amp; Operator Guide</h1><p class="muted">Purpose: understand the Noor architecture at an executive-technical level, know where the important controls live, and be able to inspect the real Firebase/Vertex configuration without drowning in implementation detail.</p><div class="callout"><b>Core design:</b> Noor retrieves approved Quran/tafsir evidence before generation. The model can synthesize naturally, but it should not make unsupported religious claims. Specific failures become eval cases; general failure classes become reusable runtime capabilities.</div><h2>1. System architecture</h2><div class="flow">User question + validated conversation state
  ↓
Auth / App Check / entitlement / quota / idempotency
  ↓
Query understanding + contextual rewrite
  ↓
Hybrid retrieval (Vertex semantic embeddings + lexical search)
  ↓
Ranking / deduplication / source balancing
  ↓
Answerability — can the evidence really answer?
  ↓
Selected evidence blocks (S1, S2, ...)
  ↓
Grounded generation with Gemini
  ↓
Structural + citation + generic answer-quality validation
  ↓
ANSWER / INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE / POLICY_REFUSAL / TEMPORARY_FAILURE</div><h2>2. Key components</h2><table><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Job</th><th>Primary code</th></tr><tr><td>Access boundary</td><td>Validate request, Auth, App Check, entitlement, quota and idempotency.</td><td><code>validation.ts</code>, <code>policy.ts</code>, <code>entitlement.ts</code>, <code>usage.ts</code>, <code>handler.ts</code></td></tr><tr><td>Query understanding</td><td>Direct question vs follow-up, subject preservation/switching, anaphora.</td><td><code>queryRewrite.ts</code></td></tr><tr><td>Retrieval</td><td>Semantic vector + lexical retrieval, fusion, ranking and deduplication.</td><td><code>embedding.ts</code>, <code>retrieval.ts</code>, <code>lexical.ts</code></td></tr><tr><td>Answerability</td><td>Separate evidence that is merely similar from evidence that can answer.</td><td><code>handler.ts</code></td></tr><tr><td>Generation</td><td>Turn bounded evidence into a grounded conversational answer.</td><td><code>generation.ts</code></td></tr><tr><td>Citations / quality</td><td>Ensure citation IDs resolve to retrieved evidence and output remains grounded.</td><td><code>citations.ts</code>, <code>generation.ts</code>, <code>handler.ts</code></td></tr><tr><td>Callable API</td><td>Firebase callable boundary used by the iOS app.</td><td><code>callable.ts</code></td></tr></table><h2>3. Knowledge-base pipeline</h2><p>Reviewed source coverage currently comes from Ibn Kathir (abridged English) and Al-Sa'di Arabic tafsir.</p><div class="flow">Reviewed tafsir files → normalize → canonical units → chunks → lookups → exact-token promotion → 768-d embeddings → Firestore corpus</div><p><b>Local deterministic artifact:</b> 9,057 chunks, hash <code>f6efa40d...adbca5</code>.<br><b>Production promoted artifact:</b> 9,248 chunks, hash <code>5fadc4e1...f1ab528</code>. Same source material; production Vertex token counting creates additional splits above the 1,400-token ceiling.</p><h2>4. High-value configuration</h2><table><tr><th>Setting</th><th>Value</th></tr><tr><td>Firebase project</td><td><code>qurannotes-9f7a1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Callable</td><td><code>askNoorRagV1</code>, <code>us-central1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Corpus version</td><td><code>2026-08-10-v1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Embedding model</td><td><code>gemini-embedding-2</code></td></tr><tr><td>Embedding dimension</td><td><code>768</code></td></tr><tr><td>Generation model</td><td><code>gemini-3.5-flash-lite</code></td></tr><tr><td>Semantic top-K</td><td><code>8</code></td></tr><tr><td>Ibn Kathir threshold</td><td><code>0.72</code></td></tr><tr><td>Al-Sa'di threshold</td><td><code>0.76</code></td></tr><tr><td>Known-good stable tag</td><td><code>noor-rag-stable-v1</code></td></tr></table><h2>5. Verification harness</h2><table><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Command</th><th>What it proves</th></tr><tr><td>Structural / deterministic</td><td><code>npm run noor:verify</code></td><td>Corpus integrity, tests, build/contracts and deterministic exact cases.</td></tr><tr><td>Real semantic retrieval</td><td><code>npm run noor:verify:retrieval</code></td><td>Real Vertex embeddings against the promoted Firestore corpus without generation.</td></tr><tr><td>Authenticated live</td><td><code>npm run noor:verify:live</code></td><td>Auth + App Check + retrieval + generation + citations + conversation-state behavior.</td></tr></table><div class="flow">stable-v1 → candidate → noor:verify → noor:verify:retrieval → targeted deployment → noor:verify:live → stable-v2 OR rollback</div><h2>6. What regression cases actually test</h2><table><tr><th>Example</th><th>General capability</th></tr><tr><td>Noah vs Nuh</td><td>Semantic equivalence and transliteration.</td></tr><tr><td>Al-Baqarah “its significance”</td><td>Contextual/anaphoric query understanding.</td></tr><tr><td>Football score</td><td>Answerability and clean abstention.</td></tr><tr><td>Riba follow-up</td><td>Sequential generation, citation validation and earned conversation state.</td></tr><tr><td>Wudu ambiguity</td><td>Generic grounded-answer quality and preservation of material qualifications, not topic-specific runtime logic.</td></tr></table><div class="callout"><b>Architecture rule:</b><br>Specific failure → eval case.<br>General failure class → reusable runtime capability.</div><h2>7. Tuning levers</h2><ol><li>Corpus quality</li><li>Chunking</li><li>Retrieval and ranking</li><li>Generation contract</li><li>Generic quality and grounding</li><li>Evals</li><li>Observability</li></ol><h2>8. Live project links</h2><ul><li><a href="https://console.firebase.google.com/project/qurannotes-9f7a1/overview">Firebase project</a></li><li><a href="https://console.firebase.google.com/project/qurannotes-9f7a1/firestore">Firestore data</a></li><li><a href="https://console.firebase.google.com/project/qurannotes-9f7a1/firestore/indexes">Firestore indexes</a></li><li><a href="https://console.firebase.google.com/project/qurannotes-9f7a1/functions">Firebase Functions</a></li><li><a href="https://console.firebase.google.com/project/qurannotes-9f7a1/appcheck">Firebase App Check</a></li><li><a href="https://console.cloud.google.com/vertex-ai?project=qurannotes-9f7a1">Vertex AI</a></li><li><a href="https://console.cloud.google.com/run?project=qurannotes-9f7a1">Cloud Run revisions</a></li><li><a href="https://console.cloud.google.com/logs/query?project=qurannotes-9f7a1">Logs Explorer</a></li></ul><h2>9. Technical references</h2><ul><li><a href="https://firebase.google.com/docs/firestore/vector-search">Firestore vector search</a></li><li><a href="https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/embeddings/get-text-embeddings">Vertex AI embeddings</a></li><li><a href="https://firebase.google.com/docs/functions/callable">Callable Cloud Functions</a></li><li><a href="https://firebase.google.com/docs/app-check">Firebase App Check</a></li></ul><p class="muted">Operator note: update stable production facts whenever an authenticated newer baseline is promoted.</p></body></html>